-- G18: the source half of the unfer amplitude-scale integration.
--
-- The admitted operation is the amplitude scale the SIRK solver applies when
-- it combines basis states (`QuantumState::scale_and_add`): every amplitude
-- multiplied by the same real factor. The factor is a source literal here
-- because the v1 bundle ABI carries arrays, not scalars; 2.5 is exactly
-- representable in both binary32 and binary64 (2.5 = 5/4), so an f32 product
-- of an f32 amplitude is exactly the f64 product of that amplitude rounded
-- once — which is what makes the bit-for-bit comparison in
-- `fock_sirk/examples/austral_pointwise.rs` meaningful instead of a tolerance
-- argument.
--
-- Float32 and `wgsl-f32-v1` are deliberate: unfer's solver state is f64, so the
-- host converts explicitly and the loss of precision is a named, measured step
-- rather than a silent reinterpretation.
module UnferScale is
    function scale(x: Float32): Float32;
end module.
